1	### Task 6: Job Seeker Home page
2	
3	**Files:**
4	- Create: `pan-african-org/en/seeker-home.html`
5	- Test: `tests/org-content.test.js`
6	
7	**Interfaces:**
8	- Consumes: the dataset conventions from Task 5.
9	- Produces: `seeker-home.html` — a page with a **different shell** from the admin console. Task 11 embeds its markup as video beat 04.
10	
11	Modelled on `org-demo.icubefarm.com/en/home`, observed logged in on 2026-08-20.
12	
13	- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing test**
14	
15	Append to `tests/org-content.test.js`:
16	
17	```js
18	test('seeker home renders the seeker shell', () => {
19	  const html = read('seeker-home.html');
20	  for (const item of ['Home', 'Inbox', 'My Career', 'Jobs', 'Entities']) {
21	    assert.ok(html.includes(`>${item}<`), `seeker nav missing "${item}"`);
22	  }
23	  assert.ok(html.includes('WhatsApp Support'), 'missing support link');
24	  assert.ok(html.includes('Settings'), 'missing settings link');
25	});
26	
27	test('seeker home renders a job feed with apply affordances', () => {
28	  const html = read('seeker-home.html');
29	  const cards = html.match(/class="[^"]*job-card[^"]*"/g) || [];
30	  assert.ok(cards.length >= 4, `expected at least 4 job cards, got ${cards.length}`);
31	  assert.ok(html.includes('CLOSES IN'), 'missing closing-date affordance');
32	  assert.ok(html.includes('Apply'), 'missing Apply action');
33	  assert.ok(html.includes('Share'), 'missing Share action');
34	});
35	
36	test('seeker home renders both quick-action panels', () => {
37	  const html = read('seeker-home.html');
38	  for (const label of [
39	    'My Career Profile', 'PDF Resume Builder', 'Web Resume Builder',
40	    'My Job Applications', 'Post Job', 'Manage Users', 'Entity Dashboard'
41	  ]) {
42	    assert.ok(html.includes(label), `quick actions missing "${label}"`);
43	  }
44	});
45	
46	test('no raw i18n key leaks on the seeker page', () => {
47	  const html = read('seeker-home.html');
48	  const body = html.slice(html.indexOf('<body'));
49	  const leaks = body.match(/>[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]*\.[A-Z0-9_.]+</g) || [];
50	  assert.deepStrictEqual(leaks, [], `raw i18n keys visible: ${leaks.join(', ')}`);
51	  assert.ok(!/myCareer\.recent/i.test(body), 'the live demo key leak must not be reproduced');
52	});
53	
54	test('seeker home carries the language toggle', () => {
55	  const html = read('seeker-home.html');
56	  assert.ok(html.includes('hreflang="fr"'), 'missing FR toggle link');
57	  assert.ok(html.includes('hreflang="es"'), 'missing ES toggle link');
58	});
59	```
60	
61	- [ ] **Step 2: Run test to verify it fails**
62	
63	Run: `node --test tests/org-content.test.js`
64	Expected: FAIL — `ENOENT ... seeker-home.html`.
65	
66	- [ ] **Step 3: Build the page**
67	
68	Create `pan-african-org/en/seeker-home.html`. Copy the `<head>` block (fonts, Phosphor icons, CSS custom properties) verbatim from `pan-african-org/en/index.html` so the design system matches, then build this structure:
69	
70	- **Top bar:** brand (organization name), inbox icon with badge, notification icon with badge, avatar, **language toggle** — for this shell the toggle lives in the top bar, not the sidebar foot
71	- **Left nav:** Home *(active)*, Inbox `5`, My Career, Jobs, Entities · footer group: WhatsApp Support, Notifications `1`, Settings, user identity block
72	- **Centre column:** "Home" heading, a "Hide announcements" control, then **at least 4** job cards, each with `class="job-card"` and containing:
73	  - job title (h3)
74	  - `CLOSES IN 8 Days`
75	  - work mode + location — e.g. `Hybrid · Addis Ababa`
76	  - employer name (a member company from the Task 5 dataset)
77	  - optional Business Unit / Department chips
78	  - `Apply` (primary) and `Share` (secondary) buttons
79	  - a `JOB` tag
80	- **Right rail:** two panels — *Professional Quick Actions* (My Career Profile, PDF Resume Builder, Web Resume Builder, My Job Applications) and *Entity Quick Actions* (member company name, then Post Job, Manage Users, Entity Dashboard)
81	
82	Use the Task 5 dataset for every employer name and location, keeping the ~70/30 Ethiopia split within the visible cards.
83	
84	- [ ] **Step 4: Run tests to verify they pass**
85	
86	Run: `node --test tests/org-content.test.js`
87	Expected: PASS
88	
89	- [ ] **Step 5: Commit**
90	
91	```bash
92	git add pan-african-org/en/seeker-home.html tests/org-content.test.js
93	git commit -m "feat(org): add job seeker home page"
94	```
